.\" sage-box(1) manpage — mdoc format
.\" Version 0.1.0
.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt SAGE-BOX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sage-box
.Nd make a Mac a Sage.is box over SSH, from one file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Op Fl -apply
.Op Fl -reboot
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Cm update
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm status
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm read
.Ar verb
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm unlock
.Op Fl -hours Ar n
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm lock
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm backup
.Op Fl -init | Fl -nightly
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Cm mailbox
.Ar args ...
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Cm manage
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Cm import push
.Ar dir name
.Nm
.Ar box
.Op Fl -as-me
.Cm tunnel install
.Fl -env-file Ar path
.Nm
.Ar box
.Cm mailbox secret
.Ar name
.Fl -from Ar bw:item[/field] | Fl -prompt Oo Fl -vault Ar item Oo Fl -replace Oc Oc | Fl -clear
.Nm
.Cm local
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A box is a Mac that runs Sage.is apps for a team.
.Nm
reads one file per box,
.Pa ~/.sage-is/boxes/<box>.env ,
reaches the box over SSH through its read key, prints what it found and what
it would change, and changes nothing. With
.Fl -apply
it runs the plan. Every step is idempotent: a second run finds everything in
place and prints
.Dq Nothing to change .
.Pp
The box file holds the box's address and login, the names of the vault items
that unlock it, and what it runs. Secrets are
.Li bw:
references, and a secret written into the file is refused.
.Xr sage-secret 1
resolves only the references a command needs, and they reach the box on
stdin, never on a command line and never on a disk here.
.Cm status
and
.Cm read
need the read key alone; a window needs nothing from the vault.
The file names a host and a login, so it stays out of every repository; the
formula installs an
example as
.Pa share/sage-box/boxes/example.env .
.Sh DOORS
Each run reaches the box through one door, each with its own key.
.Pa docs/boxes/access.md
in the tap is the standard.
.Bl -tag -width "window"
.It read
.Ev BOX_READ_KEY ,
an ed25519 key in the vault.
.Cm status ,
.Cm read
and the dry run use it, and nothing else: ssh runs with
.Li -F none
and
.Li IdentitiesOnly=yes ,
and its one IdentityFile is the read key's public half. The box's
.Pa authorized_keys
line forces the key through the read dispatcher, which answers a fixed list of
verbs. A box that refuses the key gets a message saying how to install it;
nothing falls back to the admin key.
.It backup
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_KEY ,
a second ed25519 key in the vault, for
.Cm backup
alone. ssh runs as for the read key. The box's line forces the key through
rrsync, read-only, in the staging folder
.Pa ~/.sage-is/backups/trellis-crm/current ;
it can write nothing and read nothing else.
.It window
A certificate that
.Cm unlock
signs with a person's FIDO CA, for one to four hours. Admin verbs use it while
it is valid. The box checks its principal, its addresses and its expiry.
.It me
.Fl -as-me :
the person's own SSH agent, such as a FIDO key. The access step asks for the
box's login password once, without echo.
.It legacy
.Ev BOX_SSH_KEY
and
.Ev BOX_SUDO
from the vault, with a one-line warning. They go once every box has windows.
.El
.Pp
Admin verbs
.Po
.Fl -apply ,
.Cm update ,
.Cm mailbox ,
.Cm manage ,
.Cm tunnel install
.Pc
take the first of window, me and legacy that is there. With none, the run
stops before it asks the vault for anything:
.Dq locked: run sage-box <box> unlock .
Each admin door shares one connection per run
.Pq Li ControlMaster=auto ,
with its own socket in
.Pa ~/.sage-is/ssh/ ,
so a run costs one login and one touch. A window's connection lives no longer
than the window, and
.Cm lock
closes it.
.Sh STEPS
.Bl -tag -width "registry"
.It access
The box's half of the doors, all root's: the read dispatcher
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/sage-box/read ,
the root helper
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/sage-box/root ,
and the sudoers drop-in
.Pa /etc/sudoers.d/sage-box .
It runs only when they differ from what this
.Nm
writes, and it takes the login password once: from the vault on the legacy
door, typed at a terminal on the others. An agent in a window cannot change
root's files.
.It keys
Tagged lines in the box user's
.Pa authorized_keys :
the read key, forced through the dispatcher; the backup key, when the box file
names one, forced through
.Pa ~/.sage-is/bin/sage-box-rrsync ,
which this step writes beside it; and one
.Li cert-authority
line per CA in
.Pa ~/.sage-is/ca .
That script runs brew's rrsync with brew's rsync: as brew ships it, rrsync
starts
.Pa /usr/bin/rsync ,
which on macOS is openrsync and refuses rrsync's
.Li --confine-root .
Both carry
.Li restrict
and
.Li from= Ns Ev BOX_OPERATORS .
Every line tagged
.Li sage-box:
is replaced; every other line stays as it was, except a copy of one of these
keys without its tag. A dated copy of the file comes first. A second run
changes nothing.
.It tools
.Li brew tap
and
.Li brew trust
the Sage.is and krunkit taps; install
.Nm sage-runtime ,
.Nm trellis-crm
and, when
.Ev BOX_AI_UI
is 1,
.Nm ai-ui ;
brew's
.Nm rsync
when the box file names a backup key, and
.Nm cloudflared
when it names a tunnel.
A box without Homebrew gets its signed package first.
.It runtime
A new Colima VM (krunkit on Apple Silicon) when there is none;
.Li sage-runtime convert --yes
when the VM is vz. The dry run says so first.
.It leftovers
What Docker Desktop left behind, as
.Li sage-runtime status
lists it: dangling plugin links, a
.Pa /var/run/docker.sock
that leads nowhere, a missing buildx. What the tool cannot mend it prints.
.It power
.Li pmset -a sleep 0 autorestart 1 ,
and a LaunchDaemon that starts Colima at power-on as the box user, with
nobody signed in. The root helper writes the plist itself.
.It key, checkout
Source mode only: the read-only deploy key from the vault at
.Pa ~/.ssh/trellis-deploy ,
and a clone of Sage-is/trellis at
.Ev BOX_CHECKOUT .
A refused clone prints the one
.Li gh api
line an admin runs to register the key.
.It registry
.Li docker login ghcr.io
with the token on stdin; the Trellis image is a private package.
.It trellis
.Li trellis-crm start
with the profile, URL and port from the file, from the checkout in source
mode or the image alone in image mode;
.Ev BOX_REVIEW_AT
and
.Ev BOX_SHIFT_END
go into the settings file first. Then
.Li ai-ui start
when the box runs AI-UI.
.It backups
A LaunchDaemon on the box runs
.Li trellis-crm backup --dir ~/.sage-is/backups/trellis-crm/current
nightly at 02:00. An older one is installed again. When the box's trellis-crm
has no
.Li backup --dir ,
.Fl -apply
stops here and names
.Cm update
as the fix.
.It verify
Both apps answer their health checks. When the box runs AI-UI,
.Li sage-ai
must also be on
.Li sage-network .
With
.Fl -reboot ,
the box restarts and the checks run again.
.El
.Pp
.Cm peer
mode runs the first six steps and no Trellis: a developer's Mac.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "backup --nightly"
.It Cm update
.Li brew upgrade
our tools; in source mode
.Li git pull --ff-only
in the checkout;
.Li trellis-crm update ;
.Li ai-ui start
when the box runs AI-UI, then
.Li sage-ai
joins
.Li sage-network
again; then verify.
The first step that fails stops the run.
.It Cm backup
Attach the encrypted sparse bundle
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_DIR
at
.Pa ~/.sage-is/box-backups/<box>
with its passphrase from the vault on stdin, pull the box's staging folder
through the backup key with brew's rsync into a snapshot named by the time,
then detach it. Only what changed crosses the network; every unchanged file is
a hard link to the snapshot before. A pull that breaks off leaves
.Pa <time>.partial ,
which the next pull finishes;
.Pa latest
moves only after a pull ends well. Thinning keeps every snapshot of the last 2
days, then the newest of each day to 30 days, then the newest of each week to
a year.
.It Cm backup Fl -init
Make the bundle: APFS, AES-256, sparse. Its passphrase is made here, stored
first with
.Li sage-secret put Ar item Li --stdin
under the item
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_SPARSE
names, then handed to
.Li hdiutil create -stdinpass .
An item that exists is never replaced.
.It Cm backup Fl -nightly
Install a launchd agent on this Mac that runs
.Cm backup
at 03:30, after the box's own run. It checks that the box file names the
backup key, the passphrase and the bundle.
.It Cm manage Ar command Op Ar args ...
Run
.Li trellis-crm manage
on the box, every argument as typed, its exit code back. The box runs
.Cm seed_profile ,
.Cm loaddata Ar name ,
.Cm import_sheet Pa /app/file.csv Fl -sheet Ar name Op Fl -create
and
.Cm import_incumbent Pa /app/mockups/imports/name Fl -source Ar source Op Fl -apply ,
and refuses anything else with exit 2.
.It Cm import push Ar dir name
Send the folder
.Ar dir
to a source-mode box's checkout as
.Pa mockups/imports/ Ns Ar name ,
which git ignores and Trellis reads as
.Pa /app/mockups/imports/ Ns Ar name .
It travels as base64 on stdin through the admin door, unpacks beside the old
copy and only then replaces it, at umask 077.
.It Cm tunnel install Fl -env-file Ar path
Send the env file
.Xr sage-tunnel 1
wrote, which holds the token, to
.Pa ~/.sage-is/tunnels/<name>.env
on the box on stdin, mode 600, then have the root helper load the tunnel's
LaunchDaemon. The file holds only
.Li NAME=value
lines with plain values and a
.Ev CLOUDFLARED_TUNNEL_TOKEN ;
a bad line is named by its number, never printed.
.It Cm status
Tools, VM, boot daemon, both apps, the tunnel, the age of the newest snapshot
on this Mac, and the window:
.Dq open until 14:32
or
.Dq locked .
It reads through the read key.
The
.Li ups
line comes from
.Li pmset -g ps
in the same visit:
.Li none
when no UPS is attached,
.Li <name>, 87%, on AC
or
.Li <name>, 54%, on battery
when one is, and
.Li unknown
when the box's answer cannot be read. It never fails the run.
.It Cm mailbox Ar args ...
Run
.Li trellis-crm mailbox
on the box:
.Cm list , add , check , enable , disable .
Every argument arrives as typed, and the exit code comes back: 0 ok, 1
refused, 2 usage.
A new mailbox starts disabled;
.Cm check
signs in and out and reads no mail.
A peer box has no mailboxes.
.It Cm mailbox secret Ar name Fl -from Ar bw:item[/field]
Resolve the vault item on this Mac with
.Li sage-secret run ,
the reference in a child's environment, and send the password to the box on
stdin.
.Fl -from
takes a reference only, never a password.
.It Cm mailbox secret Ar name Fl -prompt
Ask for the password twice, without echo; entries that differ change nothing.
With
.Fl -vault Ar item ,
store it first with
.Li sage-secret put Ar item Li --stdin ,
in the agents' writable organization; an item that exists needs
.Fl -replace .
Then send it as
.Fl -from
does.
When the box refuses it, the error names the
.Fl -from
line that sends it again.
.It Cm mailbox secret Ar name Fl -clear
Forget the password on the box.
.It Cm read Ar verb
One read verb through the read key, its output as the box gives it, at most 64
KiB:
.Cm probe
(what the dry run reads),
.Cm backup
(the last 50 lines of the backup log, the backup folder's dates, sizes and
names, the staging folder's database date and size and its artifact count,
and the LaunchDaemon's state),
.Cm power
.Pq Li pmset -g , pmset -g ps , uptime , No last boot ,
.Cm containers
(names and status only),
.Cm version .
The box logs every call with the tag
.Li sage-box-read .
.It Cm unlock Op Fl -hours Ar n
Make a fresh key in
.Pa ~/.sage-is/unlock/<box>/
and have the FIDO CA named by
.Ev SAGE_BOX_CA
sign it: principal
.Li sage-window ,
key ID
.Li <user>-<box>-<UTC time> ,
valid
.Ar n
hours, 1 to 4, default 2. Anything else is refused, never trimmed. The
certificate carries no forwarding and the
.Ev BOX_OPERATORS
addresses. Signing takes a touch.
.It Cm lock
Delete the window's key and close its shared connection.
.It Cm local
The tool and runtime checks on this Mac, with no SSH.
.El
.Sh SUDO
Every step that needs root calls the root helper with one fixed verb:
.Li sudo -n /usr/local/libexec/sage-box/root Ar verb .
The sudoers drop-in allows that helper with those verbs and nothing else, with
no password, so no password travels and no cached grant is needed. The helper
takes no other argument and writes every file it installs from its own text.
Its verbs:
.Cm homebrew ,
.Cm power ,
.Cm boot-daemon ,
.Cm backup-daemon ,
.Cm tunnel-daemon ,
.Cm docker-sock ,
.Cm reboot .
Only the access step uses the login password, once, to install the helper.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "SAGE_BOX_CA_DIR"
.It Ev SAGE_BOX_CA
The handle of your FIDO CA key
.Pq Li ed25519-sk No or Li ecdsa-sk ,
for
.Cm unlock .
Its
.Pa .pub
must be in the CA folder.
.It Ev SAGE_BOX_CA_DIR
The CA folder; default
.Pa ~/.sage-is/ca .
.El
.Pp
Box file settings beyond the example's comments:
.Ev BOX_READ_KEY
.Pq Li bw:<box>-read-key ,
.Ev BOX_OPERATORS
(the addresses operators reach boxes from, such as
.Li 100.64.0.0/10 ) ,
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_KEY
.Pq Li bw:<box>-backup-key ,
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_SPARSE
.Pq Li bw:<box>-backup-sparse ,
.Ev BOX_BACKUP_DIR
(the bundle's absolute path, ending in
.Pa .sparsebundle ;
it may hold spaces),
.Ev BOX_TUNNEL
(the tunnel's name), and, on the legacy door only,
.Ev BOX_SSH_KEY
and
.Ev BOX_SUDO .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.sage-is/unlock/<box>/" -compact
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/boxes/<box>.env
The box file, mode 600.
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/ca/<name>.pub
The FIDO CAs every box trusts for windows, one per device.
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/unlock/<box>/
The window's key and certificate; folder 700, key 600.
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/ssh/
Shared-connection sockets and the read key's public half; mode 700.
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/is.sage.box-backup-<box>.plist
The nightly pull on this Mac, through the backup key.
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/box-backups/<box>
Where the bundle is attached during a pull.
.It Pa ~/.sage-is/box-backups/<box>.last
The newest snapshot's name, which
.Cm status
reads without the passphrase.
.El
.Pp
On the box, all root's:
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/sage-box/read
and
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/sage-box/root
(755), and
.Pa /etc/sudoers.d/sage-box
(440). The box user's:
.Pa ~/.sage-is/bin/sage-box-rrsync
(700), the backup key's door, and
.Pa ~/.sage-is/tunnels/<name>.env
(600), the tunnel's token.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hdiutil 1 ,
.Xr rsync 1 ,
.Xr sage-runtime 1 ,
.Xr sage-secret 1 ,
.Xr sage-tunnel 1 ,
.Xr ssh-keygen 1 ,
.Xr trellis-crm 1 ,
.Xr sshd 8
